# PROXY protocol (HAProxy v2) from the AWS mail edge.
#
# Every connection reaching these listeners arrives through the WireGuard tunnel
# from HAProxy on 34.194.247.228, which prepends a PROXY v2 header carrying the
# REAL client IP. Without this, Postfix would attribute every connection to the
# tunnel peer 10.77.0.1, collapsing Rspamd/SpamAssassin scoring, Postgrey
# greylisting and Fail2ban onto a single address.
#
# Scoped per-service ON PURPOSE. Do NOT set postscreen_upstream_proxy_protocol /
# smtpd_upstream_proxy_protocol in postfix-main.cf: that would apply globally and
# make the internal 127.0.0.1:10025 amavis reinjection listener demand a PROXY
# header it will never receive, breaking local delivery.
#
# A listener with this enabled REQUIRES a PROXY header on every connection - it
# cannot also serve plain TCP. That is why Traefik is out of the mail data path.
#
# Port 25 is fronted by postscreen (master.cf: `smtp inet ... postscreen`), so it
# takes the postscreen_ variant; 587/465 are plain smtpd and take the smtpd_ one.
# Verified 2026-07-28: the edge sends PROXY v2 on all four of 25/465/587/993.
smtp/inet/postscreen_upstream_proxy_protocol=haproxy
submission/inet/smtpd_upstream_proxy_protocol=haproxy
submissions/inet/smtpd_upstream_proxy_protocol=haproxy
